kg:note_ref25724_odd_2_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "Ernst Herzfeld first visited the site of Pasargadae in November 1905 while on an expedition from Assur (Kalat Schergat, Iraq) to Shiraz (Iran). In mid-November 1923, he conducted a preleminary campaign, completing various measured plans and drawings. Finally, a four-week session of excavations in April and May 1928, funded by the Notgemeinschaft der Deutschen Wissenschaft, was carried out by Ernst Herzfeld, assisted by the architect Friedrich Krefter." .

kg:note_ref25724_scopecontent_0_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "Additional information from Ernst Herzfeld's notebook, N-109 (Arabische Inschriften II), reads, \"[Page] 71. Pasargadae, Kyrosgrab.\"" .

kg:note_ref25724_scopecontent_1_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "Additional information from Joseph Upton's Finding Aid reads, \"Arabic No. 32: [no neg.] Pasargadae. Tomb of Cyrus, mihrāb. Four sections, numbered 32/32c. See N-109, p.71 and SK-IX, p.49.\"" .

kg:note_ref25725_arrangement_0_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "Papers squeezes are organized in sequential number following language scripts, which are housed in folders, and stored in metal flat files." .

