kg:note_ref9958_odd_2_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "Ernst Herzfeld first visited the site of Pasargadae in November 1905 while on an expedition from Assur (Kalat Schergat, Iraq) to Shiraz (Iran). In mid-November 1923, he conducted a preleminary campaign, completing various measured plans and drawings. Finally, a four-week session of excavations in April and May 1928, funded by the Notgemeinschaft der Deutschen Wissenschaft, was carried out by Ernst Herzfeld, assisted by the architect Friedrich Krefter." .

kg:note_ref9958_scopecontent_0_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "- Additional information from Joseph Upton's Finding Aid reads, \"Arabic No. 33: [no neg.] Pasargadae. Tomb of Cyrus, sundial.\"" .

